## What NOT to Do (Common Mistakes)

###  Don't use this as a template to copy exactly
Every customer is different. This case is for fintech + healthcare + security SaaS. 
Your customers might be different. Adapt the methodology, don't clone the framework.

###  Don't present these artifacts to customers without context
A risk heatmap without explanation feels like finger-pointing. 
A governance roadmap without stakeholder alignment feels like you're imposing solutions.
Always start with "here's what we've learned together," not "here's what you should do."

###  Don't assume the customer wants this level of structure
Some customers are ready for quarterly risk reviews. Others still need hand-holding 
through basic onboarding. Your job is to meet them where they are, then help them 
see the value of moving to a more structured operating model.

###  Don't do this work alone
This case shows a CSM embedded with a customer's leadership. That means you need 
sales buy-in, product support, and sometimes escalation to senior leadership. 
Don't try to run a cloud trust program without organizational support.

